# Portfolio Manager —  Documentation

**Project:** Portfolio-Manager
**Type:** Full-stack investment portfolio tracking & risk analysis system
**Backend:** Java 21, Spring Boot 4.1.0 (Spring Data JDBC, Spring Data JPA, Flyway, Bean Validation)
**Frontend:** React 19 + Vite SPA
**Database:** MySQL (`portfolio_manager`)

---

## 1. Purpose

The system lets a user track investment holdings (stocks, ETFs, bonds, cash) inside a portfolio, pulling the live and historical prices from Yahoo Finance, view a dashboard of portfolio value/return/allocation, compare holding performance over selectable time ranges, and run risk analysis (volatility, max drawdown, concentration) against the portfolio. A portfolio summary can also be exported (dashboard + performance + risk combined into one response, and rendered client-side as a PDF).

There is currently no login, registration, or multi-user concept — every endpoint operates directly on a `portfolioId` path variable with no authentication layer in front of it.

