## 3. Component Breakdown

### 3.1 Frontend (`/frontend`)
A single-page React app (Vite build, not statically-served HTML/JS):
- `App.jsx` — holds the four-tab layout (`dashboard`, `holdings`, `performance`, `risk`) and the client-side PDF export logic
- `lib/api.js` — fetch wrapper (`apiRequest`) plus one function per backend endpoint; base URL resolved from `VITE_API_BASE_URL`, defaulting to `/api`
- `lib/portfolio.js` — frontend-side data shaping/helpers
- `data/demoPortfolio.js` — a demo/fallback snapshot, presumably for offline/first-load display
- Dependencies of note: `recharts` (charts), `lucide-react` (icons), `jspdf` + `jspdf-autotable` (client-generated PDF export)

### 3.2 API layer (`Controller/`)
| Controller | Base path | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `DashboardController` | `/api/portfolio/{portfolioId}/dashboard` | dashboard cards, value-over-time, sector allocation, price refresh, summary export |
| `HoldingController` | `/api/portfolio/{portfolioId}/holdings`, `/api/portfolio/holdings/{holdingId}` | list (paged), add, update quantity, delete holdings |
| `InstrumentController` | `/api/instruments` | list all available instruments |
| `MarketDataController` | `/api/market` | current price lookup and historical price import via Yahoo Finance |
| `PerformanceController` | `/api/portfolio/{portfolioId}/performance` | best/worst summary, per-holding performance, top/worst performer time series |
| `RiskAnalysisController` | `/api/risk` | portfolio volatility, max drawdown, concentration alerts |

Endpoints are documented with springdoc/OpenAPI `@Tag`/`@Operation` annotations, so Swagger UI is available.

### 3.3 Service layer (`Sevice/`)
*(the package is spelled `Sevice` throughout the codebase, not `Service` — worth an eventual rename, but every import currently depends on this spelling)*

- `HoldingService` / `HoldingServiceImpl` — holding CRUD, pagination
- `InstrumentService` / `InstrumentServiceImple` — instrument lookup
- `PerformanceService` / `PerformanceServiceImpl` — best/worst-performer summary, per-holding range return, rebased top/worst time series
- `PortfolioAnalyticsService` / `PortfolioAnalyticsServiceImpl` — dashboard aggregation (value, return, allocation, cash) and price-refresh orchestration
- `PortfolioSummaryExportService` — bundles dashboard + performance + risk into one `PortfolioSummaryExportResponse` for the export-summary endpoint
- `PriceHistoryImportService` — pulls historical closes from `YahooFinanceService` and persists them to `price_history`
- `RiskAnalysisService` — volatility (daily-return std dev, optionally annualized), max drawdown, concentration-threshold alerts; trailing 252-day lookback, minimum 20 data points before a metric is computed
- `YahooFinanceService` — live price + historical close fetch via `RestTemplate`, with a 60-second in-memory cache for live prices

### 3.4 Data layer (`Model/`, `Repository/`)
Spring Data JPA repositories over MySQL:

**Entities**
- `Portfolio` — portfolioId, name, baseCurrency, createdAt
- `Instrument` — instrumentId, ticker, name, assetClass (`STOCK`/`BOND`/`CASH`/`ETF`), sector, currency, exchange, createdAt
- `Holding` — holdingId, portfolio (FK), instrument (FK, eager-fetched), quantity, avgCost, createdAt, updatedAt
- `PriceHistory` — priceHistoryId, instrument (FK), priceDate, open/high/low/close, volume — unique on `(instrument_id, price_date)`

**Repositories:** `PortfolioRepository`, `InstrumentRepository`, `HoldingRepository`, `PriceHistoryRepository`

Schema is version-controlled via Flyway (`src/main/resources/db/migration/`): `V1__init_schema.sql`, `V2__align_existing_schema.sql`, `V3__add_price_history_table.sql`.

### 3.5 DTOs (`dto/`)
Request/response records decouple the API contract from entities — notably a rich set around performance and risk reporting:
`AddHoldingRequest`, `UpdateHoldingQuantityRequest`, `HoldingResponse`, `InstrumentResponse`, `StockPriceResponse`, `DashboardResponse` (with nested `ValuePoint` / `AllocationSlice`), `PerformanceSummaryResponse`, `PerformerSnapshotResponse`, `HoldingPerformanceResponse`, `PerformanceComparisonResponse`, `PerformancePointResponse`, `PortfolioSummaryExportResponse` (with nested `RiskSummary` / `VolatilitySummary` / `ConcentrationAlertSummary`).

